From 7d55254a588a57d2fbbb15944223da8d1ee05cb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lorenzo Giannoccaro <giannoccarol@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:03:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ims: run on Android 11

Port the stack to API 30 for the Lumia 930 (LineageOS 18.1):

- ImsService: implement the per-slot createMmTelFeature(), getConfig()
  and getRegistration() that Android 11 calls, and follow subscription
  changes with an OnSubscriptionsChangedListener, since Android 11 never
  passes the subscription to the service.
- Ready check: PhoneStateListener instead of TelephonyCallback before
  Android 12.
- Registered PLMN: fall back to the operator numeric of the service
  state when the legacy RIL reports a cell identity without MCC/MNC.
- Replace the Android 12-13 calls with their Android 11 equivalents:
  callSessionInitiatedFailed(), NetworkRegistrationInfo.isRegistered(),
  SmsManager.getSmsManagerForSubscriptionId(), SubscriptionManager
  getSubId(); skip clearCommunicationDevice() and the exact alarm check.
- Build: min_sdk_version 30, 32-bit JNI libraries linked against the NDK
  (sdk_version 30, static libc++).
